James' 2011 novel of the same name, and serves as the first
installment in the Fifty Shades film series.

15
01:00:29,032 --> 01:00:35,032
Starring Dakota Johnson, Jamie Dornan,  Jennifer Ehle and Marcia Gay Harden, the film's story follows Anastasia "Ana"
Steele, a college graduate, who begins a sadomasochistic relationship with young business magnate Christian Grey.

16
01:04:30,967 --> 01:04:36,967
Development of the film commenced in March 2012, when Universal and Focus
Features secured the rights to the trilogy following a bidding war.

17
01:08:32,903 --> 01:08:38,903
After Marcel was hired to write the film's screenplay, multiple directors, including Joe Wright, Patty
Jenkins, Bill Condon, Bennett Miller, and Steven Soderbergh, were attached to the film.

18
01:12:34,838 --> 01:12:40,838
Taylor-Johnson was confirmed as the director in June 2013.

19
01:16:36,774 --> 01:16:42,774
She cited 9½ Weeks (1986), Last Tango in Paris (1972), and Blue Is the
Warmest Colour (2013) as her inspirations for the film.

20
01:20:38,709 --> 01:20:44,709
The main cast joined the project between October and December 2013.

21
01:24:40,645 --> 01:24:46,645
Principal photography commenced in December 2013 and concluded in February 2014.

22
01:28:42,580 --> 01:28:48,580
Reshoots involving scenes between Dornan and Johnson took place
in Vancouver during the week of October 2014.

23
01:32:44,516 --> 01:32:50,516
Danny Elfman was hired to compose the film's score.

24
01:36:46,451 --> 01:36:52,451
Fifty Shades of Grey premiered at the 65th Berlin International Film Festival on February 11,
2015, and was released in IMAX formats on February 13, by Universal Pictures.

25
01:40:48,387 --> 01:40:54,387
Despite receiving generally unfavorable reviews from critics, it was an immediate box office success, breaking
numerous box office records and earning $569.7 million worldwide against a budget of $40 million.

26
01:44:50,322 --> 01:44:56,322
The soundtrack album was also successful; "Love Me like You Do", by English singer Ellie Goulding, was nominated for the Golden Globe Award for Best Original
Song, while "Earned It", by Canadian singer the Weeknd, was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Original Song at the 88th Academy Awards.

27
01:48:52,258 --> 01:48:58,258
The film was the most awarded at the 36th Golden Raspberry Awards, winning five of six
nominations, including Worst Picture (tied with Fantastic Four) and both leading roles.

28
01:52:54,193 --> 01:53:00,193
Fifty Shades of Grey was succeeded by two sequels: Fifty Shades Darker, and Fifty Shades Freed, released in 2017 and
2018, respectively, both of which received similar negative critical reception but commercial success.

